336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (software engineering. Low-code platforms enable rapid application delivery, reduce development costs, and empower business users to participate in application creation. They are particularly suitable for workflow automation, internal business tools, and small to medium-sized applications. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
337 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (Traditional application development, on the other hand, remains essential for building complex, scalable, secure, and high-performance systems. Although it requires more time, expertise, and resources, it provides unmatched flexibility and control over application architecture. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (Organizations should evaluate factors such as project complexity, customization requirements, security, budget, available expertise, and long-term maintenance before selecting an approach. In many cases, a hybrid strategy that combines low-code platforms for rapid development with traditional programming for complex components provides the best balance of speed, flexibility, and scalability. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [18]
>>
